      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "Hehe yup - that is one of the main reasons it&#39;s such a good combo. The Obsidian Fields kinda help as well, though. Managed to get the full uber-combo out once on Ra - Imbued Fire, Flesh of the Sun God, Staff of Ra, both Solar Flares, and buffs from Legacy (Inspiring Presence and Galvanise), and for a brief turn or two (before [i]somebody[/i] Disrupted the Field) managed to enjoy the benefit of all three Obsidian Fields. It was ridiculous - Ra was doing something like twelve damage with his one-point nukes, and using more than one attack per turn (one-shots plus powers, probably played a Flame Spike on more than one turn as well). It&#39;s nice when you can just sit back and kill everything without worrying about some realy horrible card coming out and smashing you to bits or breaking your stuff (or, in Omni-10&#39;s case, both at once :P).\n",
